  "build": "before: double in quaternion, box_relation, shade_prepare and Scene3D bounds; after: float plus INSIDE subtree propagation",
  "clockTicksPerSecond": 1000000,
  "isPerformanceBaseline": false,
  "findings": [
    "The R5900 FPU is single precision; a double multiply/divide/add sequence costs ~7.2 us (~1.4 us per operation), versus 0.35 us for a whole VU0 Matrix4 multiply.",
    "box_relation (~44 us) is dominated by ~40 double operations; it is most of the 53.6 us unlit pass.",
    "Diffuse adds ~52 us per pass: the double cofactor/inverse-transpose in shade_prepare plus the normal payload.",
    "Scene3D static adds ~52 us per pass over Batch: the node AABB and the render repeat box_relation for every mesh.",
    "set_euler costs ~250 us (three double sin/cos/sqrt and six double normalizations); quaternion_trs 24 us is its double normalization.",
    "scene-lit-rows: ~54 us per world update without TRS, mostly the double mesh_bounds.",
    "scene-many-nodes: ~15 clipped triangles per frame add ~10 ms; the clipper and per-vertex lighting are double as well.",
    "After float: box_relation 44.3 -> 5.9 us, quaternion_trs 23.8 -> 2.2 us, set_euler ~250 -> ~9 us (batch-lit-animated update 15.9 -> 0.58 ms).",
    "Draw per pass: unlit 53.6 -> 15.1 us, diffuse 105.5 -> 22.0 us, Scene3D static 157.3 -> 17.6 us; Scene3D is now cheaper than Batch because INSIDE subtrees skip box_relation.",
    "scene-many-nodes draw 20.5 -> 9.8 ms; ~8.7 ms of it is the ~15 clipped triangles per frame, still double in the C clipper and per-vertex lighting.",
    "Clipper in float: scene-many-nodes draw 9.84 -> 1.71 ms; in total 20.5 -> 1.71 ms since the first profile."
  ],
